::CW_U04_L07_GP_Q01::Poem plan: Mood: quiet hope. Anchor image: one porch light. Which line best matches the plan?{
~The drums exploded under the sun.#Incorrect. This creates noise and force, not quiet hope.
~The gate snarled at the crowd.#Incorrect. This creates threat, not hope.
=A small porch light waited in the rain.#Correct. The diction is quiet and the light image supports hope.
~The kitchen laughed with red balloons.#Incorrect. This feels festive, not quiet hope.
}
::CW_U04_L07_GP_Q02::Draft line: The sidewalk kept its gray fist closed, but one green word rose. What craft choices work together?{
=Personification, metaphor, and hopeful diction.#Correct. Gray fist personifies the sidewalk, green word is metaphor, and rose supports hope.
~Only rhyme and meter.#Incorrect. The line does not depend on rhyme or meter.
~Historical research and dialogue.#Incorrect. Those are not present in the line.
~A literal report with no figurative language.#Incorrect. The line is clearly figurative.
}
::CW_U04_L07_GP_Q03::Student explanation: I used the word stubborn because it shows the shoot will not give up. What is being explained?{
~A grammar error.#Incorrect. The sentence explains a craft choice, not an error.
=Diction and craft purpose.#Correct. The student connects a word choice to meaning.
~A source citation.#Incorrect. No source citation is involved.
~A character biography.#Incorrect. There is no character biography here.
}
::CW_U04_L07_GP_Q04::Poem: One porch light held its breath above the silent street. Which mood is most supported?{
~Wild celebration.#Incorrect. The line is quiet, not celebratory.
~Angry conflict.#Incorrect. No anger appears.
~Comic confusion.#Incorrect. The image is serious and quiet.
=Quiet anticipation.#Correct. Held its breath and silent street suggest waiting.
}
::CW_U04_L07_GP_Q05::Revision goal: Make the poem less random and more integrated. What should the writer do first?{
~Add unrelated images.#Incorrect. Unrelated images increase randomness.
~Remove all figurative language.#Incorrect. The goal is intentional figurative language, not none.
=Check whether each image supports the controlling mood.#Correct. Integration means craft choices work toward one effect.
~Ignore diction.#Incorrect. Diction is central to integration.
}